{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004935-time-war","id":1004935,"title":"Time War","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-18T07:57:17-08:00","id":1004935,"title":"Time War","content":"As Time Travel is now allowed by the rules, it occurs to me that a campaign of Time War might be interesting. Logically the base from which the PCs act would have to be someplace with a privileged relationship to paradox. Alternately some being like Winkle the paradox spirit might be the patron the PCs in a desperate attempt to save reality. It's my instinct that a post-apocalyptic setting for the PCs base makes the most sense. The PCs are trying to prevent the Hellworld that surrounds them.<br /> <br /> It occurs to me that many of the logical places to change time from in for Sci Fi focused time travel stories don't work so well. Example: Stopping Lincoln's death would clearly lead to a better America. However, how would it lead to an America more likely to avoid the traps of the World of Darkness? A better choice would be to kill off Andrew Jackson a couple of years before he becomes president. Then work on integrating the Cherokee into the USA as a state of the Union. Eliminating the Trail of Tears (which was a major boon to the Wyrm), the requirement of buying land with gold (a major force in promoting a slave holding aristocracy in the South, (which was a boon to the Sabbat, the Ventrue, the NWO, the Syndicate, and others) and preventing the Elimination of the Bank of the USA and the many recessions caused by the lack of a central bank( which gave the Syndicate great powers and advantages). Similarly, there would be other unlikely places to alter the timestream. Example: In spite of the Technochcy's high tech image, they've tended to slow down technology, speeding things up might shatter their plans or displace the plans of the Camarilla or others.<br /> <br /> How would you do timewar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T08:40:41-08:00","id":1004965,"title":"","content":"Two things to consider for would be mage Time Travelers.<br /> <br /> 1. Void Engineer Chrononauts. There are probably quite a lot of these guys patrolling the time stream from some distant point in the future ensuring that reality remains on the right path free from meddling by Reality Deviants. They know how things should turn out and will do everything within their power to prevent any real threats. Little changes can be offset with other changes further up the stream, but big changes will be dealt with directly.<br /> <br /> 2. Time Resident Monsters. There are creatures living in the timestream, perhaps they are the very beasts that allow time to happen in the first place. They may be residents of the Null Zones, they may be a special bread of Patern Spider trying to keep order, or they may simple be bygons that have found a home of sorts somewhere in the time steam. Think &quot;Hounds of Tindalos&quot;. Either way, frequent travellers will almost certainly attract the attention of these creatures.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, and Paradox is going to be through the roof, both kinds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:10:39-08:00","id":1005004,"title":"","content":"We're doing a time travel game and it's not that hard to get around the Paradox. Have it happen to someone else<br /> <br /> The level of Time magic required to roam across eras is very high. Not the sort of thing most characters have if you don't substantially power up starting characters. So, if the Masters are choosing the PCs as their agents, it's the folks with Time 5 who are getting zapped by the Paradox of their acts. Also, Wonders/Devices work well if used with the appropriate finesse.<br /> <br /> Another factor that we're using is making the game about mages doing mage stuff, not &quot;Let's Go Kill Hitler!!!&quot;. E.g. the world is going to end because the Bad Guys mages have a sinister plan that the PC's can thwart. Said Bad Guys thrive by causing chaos (like changing the timeline in ways that are not so nice), so preserving continuity (particulary the nicer side of it) is a goal. E.g. one character is Union scout during the Civil War. Even though he's an ardent abolitionist, and, in the present has found out about the assassination of Lincoln, the failure of Reconstruction and the Rise of Jim Crow, he hasn't ever said, &quot;I need to go back and keep Lincoln from being assassinated!&quot; Instead, he's focused on getting the plans for the Bad Guy inspired burning of NYC to the Civil War era NYC Tradition mages to keep that from happening. Which, apparently, he must've done, since that plan failed... (That's an actual historical event, by the way). So he knows he has to get back to his home era and complete his mission...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:12:44-08:00","id":1005005,"title":"","content":"I'm running a subplot where a character has been tapped for just such an operation. Ive framed it as an alliance between Wrinkle and the Oracles of Time and Space. they are operating out of the remains of a Sidereal Exalted temple outside the time stream. I am using it to present history as always changing due to actions in the present and the current paradigm. as a twist, they are about to discover that the world has &quot;ended&quot; many times and each time this has happened the collected avatars of mankind join and then reach back to alter conditions so that this does not. the Night of Fana is the most blatant example of this. the Temple, which is called the Time Travel Cafe by the awakened who work for the operation works to undercut Nephandic time magic and foolish time travel endeavors that threaten ascension. this all works very similar to the History Monks in Discworld (Thief of Time) where agents are sent out to ensure that the right things happen. i present the Nephandi as constantly trying to alter time to stop this from occurring- the cauls are a literal weapon against this process. <br /> fun historical note- the dark alliance between WWII technocrats and traditions served to create a powerful defensive countermeasure against time travelers trying to kill hitler. time travel to that era is HARD, and rife with danger","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>there are no bad ideas, just ideas that have not been refined enough","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1608-iamthesweeper","name":"IAmTheSweeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T12:58:42-08:00","id":1005070,"title":"","content":"A Talisman made with Prime 5 and Time 5 could do it. Have it include a 'charge up time' where you have to leave it at a node, where it siphons off quintessence every day, converting that with Prime 5 into paradox warding. Until after X amount of time, it's paradox wards are sufficient to make the time jump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T13:22:25-08:00","id":1005079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004935-time-war?p=1005070#post1005070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Talisman made with Prime 5 and Time 5 could do it. Have it include a 'charge up time' where you have to leave it at a node, where it siphons off quintessence every day, converting that with Prime 5 into paradox warding. Until after X amount of time, it's paradox wards are sufficient to make the time jump.</div> </div> </div> </div>add Spirit 4 and you've got yourself an episode of Sliders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T12:30:05-08:00","id":1005436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004935-time-war?p=1004965#post1004965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two things to consider for would be mage Time Travelers.<br /> <br /> 1. Void Engineer Chrononauts. There are probably quite a lot of these guys patrolling the time stream from some distant point in the future ensuring that reality remains on the right path free from meddling by Reality Deviants. They know how things should turn out and will do everything within their power to prevent any real threats. Little changes can be offset with other changes further up the stream, but big changes will be dealt with directly.<br /> <br /> 2. Time Resident Monsters. There are creatures living in the timestream, perhaps they are the very beasts that allow time to happen in the first place. They may be residents of the Null Zones, they may be a special bread of Patern Spider trying to keep order, or they may simple be bygons that have found a home of sorts somewhere in the time steam. Think &quot;Hounds of Tindalos&quot;. Either way, frequent travellers will almost certainly attract the attention of these creatures.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, and Paradox is going to be through the roof, both kinds.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I'd either give them Winkle for a patron and/or have them come from a period from after a hellish and brutal collapse. Either way, I'd give them a privileged relationship to paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T12:32:53-08:00","id":1005438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004935-time-war?p=1005004#post1005004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're doing a time travel game and it's not that hard to get around the Paradox. Have it happen to someone else<br /> <br /> The level of Time magic required to roam across eras is very high. Not the sort of thing most characters have if you don't substantially power up starting characters. So, if the Masters are choosing the PCs as their agents, it's the folks with Time 5 who are getting zapped by the Paradox of their acts. Also, Wonders/Devices work well if used with the appropriate finesse.<br /> <br /> Another factor that we're using is making the game about mages doing mage stuff, not &quot;Let's Go Kill Hitler!!!&quot;. E.g. the world is going to end because the Bad Guys mages have a sinister plan that the PC's can thwart. Said Bad Guys thrive by causing chaos (like changing the timeline in ways that are not so nice), so preserving continuity (particulary the nicer side of it) is a goal. E.g. one character is Union scout during the Civil War. Even though he's an ardent abolitionist, and, in the present has found out about the assassination of Lincoln, the failure of Reconstruction and the Rise of Jim Crow, he hasn't ever said, &quot;I need to go back and keep Lincoln from being assassinated!&quot; Instead, he's focused on getting the plans for the Bad Guy inspired burning of NYC to the Civil War era NYC Tradition mages to keep that from happening. Which, apparently, he must've done, since that plan failed... (That's an actual historical event, by the way). So he knows he has to get back to his home era and complete his mission...</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, just as their would be things to change, their would be so many things to leave alone. Besides, why crudely kill Hitler. Stealing the child and having him raised by mentally stable parents in a stable and loving environment would accomplish the same things with far less evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T23:03:29-08:00","id":1005615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004935-time-war?p=1005438#post1005438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point, just as their would be things to change, their would be so many things to leave alone. Besides, why crudely kill Hitler. Stealing the child and having him raised by mentally stable parents in a stable and loving environment would accomplish the same things with far less evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or some other guy fills the role. If something is for a long time, or is strongly ingrained in the collective consciousness then it is difficult to circumvent. <br /> Some explain cosmological constants this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T00:14:09-08:00","id":1005630,"title":"","content":"Since Cross time travel explicitly exists and thus the multiverse theory I'd argue you can only make new timelines vs true changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T05:23:15-08:00","id":1005671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004935-time-war?p=1005615#post1005615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or some other guy fills the role. If something is for a long time, or is strongly ingrained in the collective consciousness then it is difficult to circumvent.<br /> Some explain cosmological constants this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Primally-charged (AKA Enchanted) nuke at a Nazi rally works so much better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T06:39:43-08:00","id":1005689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ld